          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            Here we discuss the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integration"} integration
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+form"} differential form
            (possibly twisted in some way) on a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+manifold"} topological manifold
            (possibly with additional structure) over an appropriately structured
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/submanifold"} submanifold
            (or
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+linear+combination"} formal linear combination
            thereof).
          %h2#Description Description
          %p
            See at
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+form"} differential form
            for basic definitions.
          %h3#integration_of_topdimension_pseudoforms_pseudoforms_to_measures Integration of top-dimension pseudoforms (pseudoforms to measures)
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            be an
            = succeed "-dimensional" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+manifold"} topological manifold
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ω
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega
            be a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+map"} continuous
            = succeed "-pseudoform" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/paracompact+space"} paracompact
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hausdorff+space"} Hausdorff
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+finite+cover"} locally finite cover
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            with a subordinate
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/partition+of+unity"} partition of unity
            and a continuous coordinate chart on each patch. (When
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differentiable+manifold"} differentiable
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} smooth
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ω
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega
            defines a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/measure+space"} measure
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            as follows:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                On each coordinate patch
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi U
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ω
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega
                into an untwisted
                = succeed "-form" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
                = succeed ";" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mover
                          %mi ω
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat{\omega}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mover
                        %mi ω
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat{\omega}
                in coordinates as
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mover
                        %mi ω
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                      %mo =
                      %msub
                        %mi ω
                        %mi U
                      %mo ∧
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} d
                      %msup
                        %mi x
                        %mn 1
                      %mo ∧
                      %mi ⋯
                      %mo ∧
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} d
                      %msup
                        %mi x
                        %mi n
                      %mo .
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat{\omega} = \omega_U \wedge \mathrm{d}x^1 \wedge \cdots \wedge \mathrm{d}x^n .
              %p In this situation, it is convenient also to write
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ω
                      %mo =
                      %msub
                        %mi ω
                        %mi U
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} d
                      %msup
                        %mi x
                        %mn 1
                      %mi ⋯
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} d
                      %msup
                        %mi x
                        %mi n
                      %mo ;
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega = \omega_U \mathrm{d}x^1 \cdots \mathrm{d}x^n ;
              %p
                in other words, we interpret
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} d
                      %msup
                        %mi x
                        %mn 1
                      %mi ⋯
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} d
                      %msup
                        %mi x
                        %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{d}x^1 \cdots \mathrm{d}x^n
                as the absolute value of
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} d
                        %msup
                          %mi x
                          %mn 1
                        %mo ∧
                        %mi ⋯
                        %mo ∧
                        %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} d
                        %msup
                          %mi x
                          %mi n
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{d}x^1 \wedge \cdots \wedge \mathrm{d}x^n
            %li
              %p
                The coordinates on
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
                define a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diffeomorphism"} diffeomorphism
                between
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
                and an open subset of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi R
                        %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{R}^n
                that we'll also call
                = succeed ";" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi U
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
              #eq:absvalposs.maruku-equation
                %span.maruku-eq-number (1)
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mo ∫
                        %mi U
                      %mi ω
                      %mo =
                      %msub
                        %mo ∫
                        %mi U
                      %msub
                        %mi ω
                        %mi U
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msup
                        %mi x
                        %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mi …
                      %mo ,
                      %msup
                        %mi x
                        %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} d
                      %msup
                        %mi x
                        %mn 1
                      %mi ⋯
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} d
                      %msup
                        %mi x
                        %mi n
                      %mo ,
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \int_U \omega = \int_U \omega_U(x^1,\ldots,x^n)\, \mathrm{d}x^1 \cdots \mathrm{d}x^n ,
              %p
                where the right-hand side is now interpreted in the usual way as an integral with respect to
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lebesgue+measure"} Lebesgue measure
            %li
              %p Using the partition of unity, write
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ω
                      %mo =
                      %munder
                        %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                        %mi U
                      %msub
                        %mi w
                        %mi U
                      %msub
                        %mi ω
                        %mi U
                      %mo ,
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega = \sum_U w_U \omega_U ,
              %p
                where
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi w
                        %mi U
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} w_U
                is a weight function defined on
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
                and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi ω
                        %mi U
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega_U
                is the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/restriction"} restriction
                of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ω
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega
                to
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi U
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                        %msub
                          %mo ∫
                          %mi X
                        %mi ω
                        %mo =
                        %msub
                          %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                          %mi U
                        %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                          %msub
                            %mo ∫
                            %mi U
                          %msub
                            %mi w
                            %mi U
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msup
                            %mi x
                            %mn 1
                          %mo ,
                          %mi …
                          %mo ,
                          %msup
                            %mi x
                            %mi n
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %msub
                            %mi ω
                            %mi U
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msup
                            %mi x
                            %mn 1
                          %mo ,
                          %mi …
                          %mo ,
                          %msup
                            %mi x
                            %mi n
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                          %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} d
                          %msup
                            %mi x
                            %mn 1
                          %mi ⋯
                          %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} d
                          %msup
                            %mi x
                            %mi n
                          %mo ,
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \textstyle{\int}_X \omega = \sum_U \textstyle{\int}_U w_U(x^1,\ldots,x^n) \omega_U(x^1,\ldots,x^n)\, \mathrm{d}x^1 \cdots \mathrm{d}x^n ,
              %p or more generally,
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                        %msub
                          %mo ∫
                          %mi E
                        %mi ω
                        %mo =
                        %msub
                          %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                          %mi U
                        %msub
                          %mo ∫
                          %mi U
                        %msub
                          %mi χ
                          %mi E
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msup
                          %mi x
                          %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %mi …
                        %mo ,
                        %msup
                          %mi x
                          %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %msub
                          %mi w
                          %mi U
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msup
                          %mi x
                          %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %mi …
                        %mo ,
                        %msup
                          %mi x
                          %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %msub
                          %mi ω
                          %mi U
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msup
                          %mi x
                          %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %mi …
                        %mo ,
                        %msup
                          %mi x
                          %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} d
                        %msup
                          %mi x
                          %mn 1
                        %mi ⋯
                        %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} d
                        %msup
                          %mi x
                          %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \textstyle{\int}_E \omega = \sum_U \int_U \chi_E(x^1,\ldots,x^n) w_U(x^1,\ldots,x^n) \omega_U(x^1,\ldots,x^n)\, \mathrm{d}x^1 \cdots \mathrm{d}x^n
              %p
                for
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi E
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
                a measurable subset of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi χ
                        %mi E
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \chi_E
                the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/characteristic+function"} characteristic function
                of
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi E
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ω
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega
                into a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/measure"} measure
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ω
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mi E
                      %mo ↦
                      %msub
                        %mo ∫
                        %mi E
                      %mi ω
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega \colon E \mapsto \int_E \omega
                on
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          %p
            %em> A priori
            , this definition depends not only on the particular coordinate patches chosen but also on the partition of unity chosen to go with them. Furthermore, the definition could be done just as easily (perhaps even more easily) for something other than an
            = succeed "-pseudoform." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
          #IntegrationTheorem.num_theorem
            %h6#theorem Theorem
            %p
              When
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ω
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega
              is an
              = succeed "-pseudoform," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mo ∫
                      %mi E
                    %mi ω
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \int_E \omega
              is independent of the coordinates and partition chosen. Furthermore, the map from
              = succeed "-pseudoforms" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
          %p
            Note that, if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ω
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega
            were an
            = succeed "-form" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %msub
                      %mi ω
                      %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {|\omega_U|}
            in place of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ω
                    %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega_U
            in
            %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:absvalposs"} (1)
            and the following equations, but then the map from forms to measures would not be linear.
          %h3#measures_to_pseudoforms Measures to pseudoforms
          %p
            It may also be enlightening to consider how to go back from a measure to an
            = succeed "-pseudoform." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ω
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega
            is an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/absolutely+continuous+measure"} absolutely continuous
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Radon+measure"} Radon measure
            on
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            = succeed "-pseudoform" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            = succeed ")" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ω
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega
          %ul
            %li
              Given a point
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi a
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi a
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a
            %li
              Given
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              linearly independent vectors
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi v
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mi …
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi v
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (v_1,\ldots,v_n)
              at
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi a
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi a
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a
            %li
              For sufficiently large natural number
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_k
              of points with coordinates in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi k
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [0,1/k]^n
              exists (lies within
              = succeed ")." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            %li
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
              be
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi lim
                        %mrow
                          %mi k
                          %mo →
                          %mn ∞
                      %msup
                        %mi k
                        %mi n
                      %mi ω
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi C
                        %mi k
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lim_{k \to \infty} k^n \omega(C_k)
            %li
              If the coordinate system on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
              is positively oriented at
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi a
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ω
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi v
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mi …
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi v
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega(v_1,\ldots,v_n)
              be
              = succeed ";" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi L
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
              is negatively oriented at
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi a
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ω
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi v
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mi …
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi v
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega(v_1,\ldots,v_n)
              be
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mi L
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} -L
            %li
              Extend the definition to
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              arbitrary vectors by continuity (which necessarily maps a linearly dependent tuple of vectors to zero).
          %p
            Again, this definition is independent of the coordinate system chosen (as long as it extends the given vectors); or if that's not true, then we messed up and need to add further restrictions to the absolutely continuous Radon measure
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ω
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega
            %em not
            independent of the orientation chosen, of course; thus we get a pseudoform rather than an untwisted form. You might try to ignore the orientation and take
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ω
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi v
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mi …
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi v
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega(v_1,\ldots,v_n)
            to be
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi L
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
            always, but that does not define an exterior form, as is most easily seen if two vectors are switched (which does not change
            = succeed ")." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/absolute+differential+form"} absolute differential form
            (which is equivalent to a pseudoform when, as here, the degree equals the dimension).
          %h3#integration_of_more_general_forms Integration of more general forms
          %p
            One can integrate forms other than
            = succeed "-pseudoforms," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            is a
            = succeed "-dimensional" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/submanifold"} submanifold
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            (that is a
            = succeed "-dimensional" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            equipped with a map
            = succeed ")," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi U
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R\colon U \to X
            = succeed "-forms" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            = succeed "-pseudoforms" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            = succeed ")" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                We may integrate a
                = succeed "-form" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi p
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi η
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta
                over
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
                if
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
                is
                = succeed "," do
                  %em oriented
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
                is oriented. We pull back
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi η
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta
                from
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                to
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi U
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
                to turn
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi η
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta
                into a
                = succeed "-pseudoform," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi p
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
                = succeed "-dimensional" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi p
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi U
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            %li
              %p
                We may integrate a
                = succeed "-pseudoform" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi p
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi η
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta
                over
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
                if
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
                is
                = succeed "," do
                  %em pseudooriented
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi a
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a
                on
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi U
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                at
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi a
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R(a)
                to a local orientation of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
                at
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi a
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi a
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a
                and taking opposite orientations to opposite orientations. Then locally, we turn
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi η
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta
                into a
                = succeed "-form" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi p
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                using a local orientation on
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi U
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
                to turn that back into a
                = succeed "-pseudoform," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi p
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi U
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
          %p
            Thus, while integration of
            = succeed "-pseudoforms" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            = succeed "-forms" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            = succeed "-pseudoforms." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
          %p
            Note that, if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is thought of a submanifold of itself, then it has a natural pseudoorientation that takes each local orientation to itself, and so we recover the original definition of integration of
            = succeed "-pseudoforms" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is an oriented manifold, then it may be viewed as an oriented submanifold of itself, giving a definition of integration of
            = succeed "-forms" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          %p
            To integrate on
            %em unoriented
            submanifolds of arbitrary dimension, use
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/absolute+differential+forms"} absolute differential forms
            %em nonlinear
            differential forms, use
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cogerm+differential+forms"} cogerm differential forms
          %h3#integration_on_other_domains Integration on other domains
          %p
            One often sees the definition of integration given for
            %em parametrised
            submanifolds, that is submanifolds where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            is an open subset of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi R
                      %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{R}^p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            (as a coordinate patch in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            or as the source of a submanifold of
            = succeed ")" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            = succeed "-pseudoform" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is independent of the coordinates chosen now becomes a theorem that the integral of a parametrised submanifold is independent of the parametrisation (up to some details about orientation), which in the end returns the result that one can integrate forms over arbitrary submanifolds (given an orientation or pseudoorientation as above).
          %p
            We can also integrate on a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+linear+combination"} formal linear combination
            of submanifolds, which is handy since these are the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chains"} chains
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %span.newWikiWord
                de Rham homology
                %a{:href => "/nlab/new/de+Rham+homology"} ?
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mo ∫
                    %mrow
                      %munder
                        %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                        %mi i
                      %msub
                        %mi α
                        %mi i
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mi i
                  %mi ω
                  %mo ≔
                  %munder
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                    %mi i
                  %msub
                    %mi α
                    %mi i
                  %msub
                    %mo ∫
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mi i
                  %mi ω
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \int_{\sum_i \alpha_i U_i} \omega \coloneqq \sum_i \alpha_i \int_{U_i} \omega .
          %h2#InCohesiveHomotopyTypeTheory In cohesive homotopy-type theory
          %p
            We discuss here a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/general+abstract"} general abstract
            formulation of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+forms"} differential forms
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integration"} integration
            and the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stokes+theorem"} Stokes theorem
            in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohesive+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-toposes"} cohesive (∞,1)-toposes
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohesive+homotopy+type+theory"} cohesive homotopy type theory
            (following
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#BunkeNikolausVoelkl13"} Bunke-Nikolaus-Völkl 13, theorem 3.2
          %h3#general_definition General definition
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}
            be a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohesive+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} cohesive (∞,1)-topos
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Π
                  %mo ⊣
                  %mo ♭
                  %mo ⊣
                  %mo ♯
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\Pi \dashv \flat \dashv \sharp)
            for the defining triple of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+modalities"} adjoint modalities
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/shape+modality"} shape modality
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ⊣
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \dashv
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flat+modality"} flat modality
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ⊣
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \dashv
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sharp+modality"} sharp modality
          %p
            As usual (see at
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "cohesive+%28infinity%2C1%29-topos+--+structures#deRhamCohomology"} structures in a cohesive ∞-topos – de Rham cohomology
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Π
                    %mi dR
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Pi_{dR}
            and
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mo ♭
                      %mi dR
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \flat_{dR}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/loop+space+object"} loop space object
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            (for instance the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/delooping"} delooping
            = succeed ")" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}G
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mo ♭
                    %mi dR
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \flat_{dR}G
            is defined by the long
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+fiber+sequence"} homotopy fiber sequence
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                  %mover
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi θ
                        %mi G
                  %msub
                    %mo ♭
                    %mi dR
                  %mi G
                  %mover
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mrow
                  %mo ♭
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi G
                  %mo ⟶
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  G \stackrel{\theta_G}{\longrightarrow} \flat_{dR} G \stackrel{}{\longrightarrow} \flat \mathbf{B}G \longrightarrow \mathbf{B}G
          %p
            where the morphism on the right is the
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ♭
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \flat
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/counit+of+a+comonad"} counit
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi θ
                    %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \theta_G
            is the
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Maurer-Cartan+form"} Maurer-Cartan form
            on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
          %blockquote
            %p
              (Beware that elsewhere we write
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mo ♭
                      %mi dR
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \flat_{dR}\mathbf{B}G
              for what here we write
              = succeed ".)" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mo ♭
                        %mi dR
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \flat_{dR}G
          %p
            Dually
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Π
                    %mi dR
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Pi_{dR}
            is defined.
          %p Write now
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Stab
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi T
                    %mo *
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi T
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                  %mo →
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  Stab(\mathbf{H}) = T_\ast \mathbf{H} \hookrightarrow T \mathbf{H} \to \mathbf{H}
          %p
            for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tangent+cohesive+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} tangent cohesive (∞,1)-topos
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stabilization"} stabilization
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Stab
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Stab(\mathbf{H})
            given by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectrum+objects"} spectrum objects
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}
          %p
            We assume that there is an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/interval+object"} interval object
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo *
                  %mo ∪
                  %mo *
                  %mover
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi i
                        %mn 0
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi i
                        %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %msup
                    %mi Δ
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\ast \cup \ast \stackrel{(i_0, i_1)}{\longrightarrow}  \Delta^1
          %p
            “exhibiting the cohesion” (see at
            = succeed ")" do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuum"} continuum
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence"} equivalence
            between the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/shape+modality"} shape modality
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Π
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Pi
            and the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/localization+of+an+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} localization
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi L
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi Δ
                        %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_{\Delta^1}
            at the the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/projection"} projection
            maps out of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+products"} Cartesian products
            with this line
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi Δ
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ×
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta^1\times (-) \to (-)
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Π
                  %mo ≃
                  %msub
                    %mi L
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi Δ
                        %mn 1
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\Pi \simeq L_{\Delta^1}
                  \\,.
          %p
            This is the case for instance for the “standard
            = succeed "\u201D," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuum"} continuum
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+line"} real line
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                  %mo =
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H} =
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Smooth%E2%88%9EGrpd"} Smooth∞Grpd
          %p
            It follows in particular that there is a chosen
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-categories"} equivalence of (∞,1)-categories
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ♭
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≃
                  %msub
                    %mi L
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi Δ
                        %mn 1
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\flat(\mathbf{H})\simeq L_{\Delta^1}\mathbf{H}
          %p
            between the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flat+modality"} flat
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modal+types"} modal homotopy-types
            and the
            = succeed "-homotopy" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta^1
          %p
            Given a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+homotopy+type"} stable homotopy type
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi E
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi Stab
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi T
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat E \in Stab(\mathbf{H})\hookrightarrow T \mathbf{H}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohesion"} cohesion
            provides two objects
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Π
                    %mi dR
                  %mover
                    %mi E
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %msub
                    %mo ♭
                    %mi dR
                  %mover
                    %mi E
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi Stab
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\Pi_{dR} \hat E \,,\;\;  \flat_{dR}\hat E
                  \\;\;
                  \\in Stab(\mathbf{H})
          %p
            which may be interpreted as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/de+Rham+complexes"} de Rham complexes
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coefficients"} coefficients
            in
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Π
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mo ♭
                      %mi dR
                    %mi Σ
                    %mover
                      %mi E
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Pi(\flat_{dR} \Sigma \hat E)
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mi Π
                            %mi dR
                          %mover
                            %mi E
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo ⟶
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi d
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mo ♭
                            %mi dR
                          %mover
                            %mi E
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mrow
                            %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                              %mi ι
                          %mo ↘
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mo ↗
                            %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi θ
                                  %mover
                                    %mi E
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mi E
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  \\Pi_{dR}\hat E &amp;&amp; \stackrel{\mathbf{d}}{\longrightarrow} &amp;&amp; \flat_{dR}\hat E
                  \\\
                  \&amp; {}_{\mathllap{\iota}}\searrow &amp;&amp; \nearrow_{\mathrlap{\theta_{\hat E}}}
                  \\\
                  \&amp;&amp;
                  \\hat E
                  }
          %p
            which interprets as the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/de+Rham+differential"} de Rham differential
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi d
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{d}
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+cohomology+diagram"} differential cohomology diagram
            for details.
          %p
            Throughout in the following we leave the “inclusion”
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ι
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \iota
            of “differential forms regarded as
            = succeed "-connections" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi E
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat E
            = succeed "-bundles\u201D" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
          #CohesiveIntegrationOfDifferentialForms.num_defn
            %h6#definition Definition
            %p
              %em Integration of differential
              forms is the morphism
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mo ∫
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi Δ
                          %mn 1
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mo ♭
                      %mi dR
                    %mover
                      %mi E
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ⟶
                    %msub
                      %mi Π
                      %mi dR
                    %mover
                      %mi E
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\int_{\Delta^1} \;\colon\;  [\Delta^1, \flat_{dR}\hat E] \longrightarrow \Pi_{dR}\hat E
            %p
              which is induced via the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+cofiber"} homotopy cofiber
              property of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mo ♭
                      %mi dR
                    %mi Ω
                    %mover
                      %mi E
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \flat_{dR}\Omega \hat E
              from the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/counit+of+a+comonad"} counit
              naturality square of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flat+modality"} flat modality
              on
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo *
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                      %mo *
                      %mover
                        %mo →
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msub
                            %mi i
                            %mn 0
                          %mo ,
                          %msub
                            %mi i
                            %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %msup
                        %mi Δ
                        %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ,
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [(\ast \coprod \ast \stackrel{(i_0, i_1)}{\to} \Delta ^1 ), -]
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/null+homotopy"} null homotopy
              due to the
              = succeed "-homotopy" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi Δ
                        %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta^1
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo ♭
                      %mover
